<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
Hardened-runtime entitlements required for notarization (notarytool refuses
to notarize a build without the hardened runtime enabled, and the hardened
runtime refuses to run unless the specific things it locks down are
explicitly re-opened here).

- allow-unsigned-executable-memory / disable-library-validation: PyInstaller
  bundles a Python interpreter plus a pile of compiled extension modules
  (pyobjc's .so/.dylib files, etc.) that are not all signed by the same Team
  ID as this app -- without disable-library-validation, the hardened runtime
  refuses to load them at all and the app crashes on launch.
- automation.apple-events: pyobjc's Accessibility (AXUIElement) and
  Quartz/CGWindowList calls go through Apple Events/private frameworks under
  the hood; without this the OS can silently deny calls that would otherwise
  look identical to a permissions bug.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
